<!--
  The clasp.

  Traced from the line drawing the household chose, not redrawn from primitives — four
  attempts at rebuilding it out of rounded rectangles produced a mitten every time. A
  drawn hand has curves that a rectangle rotated 45 degrees cannot fake, so the artwork
  is the artwork, vectorised.

  Line art rather than filled shapes, which suits this app: every screen in Ours is
  built from hairlines, and it means the monochrome layer below is the same path with
  nothing removed. A two-tone illustration would have collapsed into one mass the moment
  Android themed it.

  Sized to 62 in a 108 viewport, so the whole mark sits inside the 72 the launcher mask
  guarantees — it survives a circle, a squircle and a rounded square without cropping.
-->
